          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Connecting an ecosystem that spans **MYOB Acumatica**, **SAP**, dedicated **CRM platforms** (like Salesforce, HubSpot, or Dynamics 365), and **Microsoft 365** requires specialists who understand both mid-market and enterprise architectures, as well as modern iPaaS (Integration Platform as a Service) middleware such as Boomi or Azure Integration Services.\n\nThe leading system integration consultancies in Perth with direct expertise in these environments are categorized below based on their primary platform strengths:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Atturra (Perth Office)\n* **Best for:** Enterprise-grade middleware, complex SAP integrations, and multi-system iPaaS.\n* **Overview:** Atturra (ASX: ATA) is one of Australia’s premier data and system integration providers. They are the top Boomi partner in the Asia-Pacific region and hold top-tier Microsoft partner credentials. \n* **Relevant Strengths:** If your architecture involves orchestrating high-volume transactions between **SAP**, **CRM platforms**, and **Microsoft 365 / Azure**, Atturra has the deepest onshore technical team in Perth to deploy governed, scalable middleware (Boomi, Azure Logic Apps, and API Management).\n\n### 2. Stratus Consulting Group (incorporating Horizon Business Systems)\n* **Best for:** MYOB Acumatica core ERP integrations and CRM sync.\n* **Overview:** Stratus Group was formed in part by Perth-based **Horizon Business Systems**, one of Western Australia’s longest-standing ERP partners. They are a perennial MYOB Diamond Partner and ANZ Partner of the Year winner.\n* **Relevant Strengths:** They are specialists in **MYOB Acumatica** implementations and custom integrations. If MYOB Acumatica is the hub of your business, Stratus specializes in connecting its REST APIs to external CRMs (Salesforce, HubSpot), Microsoft 365, and downstream operational software.\n\n### 3. Velrada (an NRI Company)\n* **Best for:** Microsoft-centric ecosystems, Dynamics 365 CRM, and SAP-to-Azure connectivity.\n* **Overview:** Headquartered in Perth, Velrada is one of Australia’s most celebrated Microsoft Solutions Partners.\n* **Relevant Strengths:** Velrada specializes in using **Microsoft 365, Power Platform, Azure Logic Apps, and Dynamics 365** as the central nervous system of an organization. They regularly deliver enterprise projects integrating Microsoft cloud tools with core ERP engines like **SAP** (both ECC and S/4HANA).\n\n### 4. Leverage Technologies\n* **Best for:** Multi-ERP cross-competence (SAP Business One + MYOB Acumatica).\n* **Overview:** Leverage Technologies is unique in Australia for running tier-1 implementation and development practices across **both SAP (specifically SAP Business One) and MYOB Acumatica**.\n* **Relevant Strengths:** If your business is running both SAP and MYOB Acumatica (e.g., across separate subsidiaries, divisions, or supply chains) and needs them aligned with common CRM and Microsoft 365 workflows, Leverage Technologies has native expertise in both ecosystems without needing two separate vendors.\n\n### 5. Metisc (Perth)\n* **Best for:** Mid-market Microsoft 365 / Dynamics CRM integrations with external ERPs.\n* **Overview:** A Perth-based consultancy with over 25 years of experience specializing in Microsoft Cloud solutions, Dynamics 365, and application integration.\n* **Relevant Strengths:** Metisc builds pre-configured and custom API connectors to bridge **Microsoft 365 / Dynamics CRM** with local accounting and ERP engines like MYOB and external SQL/ERP databases.\n\n---\n\n### How to Choose Among Them\n\n| Primary Scenario | Recommended Partner |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **You run SAP + complex CRM/cloud pipelines** and need a dedicated middleware solution (Boomi / MuleSoft / Azure). | **Atturra** |\n| **MYOB Acumatica is your primary ERP**, and you need it integrated into CRM and M365 without custom code fragility. | **Stratus Consulting Group** |\n| **Microsoft 365 / Power Platform / Dynamics is your driver**, and you need to feed it data from an existing SAP system. | **Velrada** |\n| **You operate a hybrid environment** using both SAP Business One and MYOB Acumatica across business units. | **Leverage Technologies** |\n\n**Key architectural tip:** Because MYOB Acumatica, SAP, and modern CRMs operate at differing API rate limits and data models, ensure your selected partner assesses whether you need an **iPaaS / message bus (like Azure Service Bus or Boomi)** to prevent sync locks and failed transactions between your financial and customer systems.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
          "role": "model"
